07:38:16,680 --> 07:38:20,880
not have to go through other people's calls and you can leverage theirs, but your calls

9030
07:38:20,880 --> 07:38:22,120
just get way better.

9031
07:38:22,120 --> 07:38:25,590
And you stop tripping over yourself when you talk about the same things.

9032
07:38:25,590 --> 07:38:27,950
Okay, that's part two.

9033
07:38:27,950 --> 07:38:29,430
Part three is support.

9034
07:38:29,430 --> 07:38:34,790
Basically, we have a lot of customers and a lot of them need support.

9035
07:38:34,790 --> 07:38:39,910
And right now, there are not enough people to support all of those customers on their own,

9036
07:38:39,910 --> 07:38:40,910
just one on one.

9037
07:38:40,910 --> 07:38:43,150
So you need to be able to scale up your support.

9038
07:38:43,150 --> 07:38:45,990
And a lot of founders leave this to the very last thing,

9039
07:38:45,990 --> 07:38:47,270
believe me, I've been there.

9040
07:38:47,270 --> 07:38:49,270
And it makes your life very, very tough

9041
07:38:49,270 --> 07:38:51,950
to handle both getting new customers through the funnel

9042
07:38:51,950 --> 07:38:54,110
and then also supporting the preexisting ones.

9043
07:38:54,110 --> 07:38:55,590
And so you have a real opportunity

9044
07:38:55,590 --> 07:38:57,390
to automate this with Rockbot.

9045
07:38:57,390 --> 07:39:00,550
But the most important part that makes this really work well

9046
07:39:00,550 --> 07:39:03,590
is that you spend the time empowering your bot

9047
07:39:03,590 --> 07:39:05,830
to actually support your customers.

9048
07:39:05,830 --> 07:39:08,470
And what that means is you not only connect it to your data,

9049
07:39:08,470 --> 07:39:09,670
but you connect it to your billing.

9050
07:39:09,670 --> 07:39:13,910
And you connect it to the risky pieces that you're scared to give because that is where

9051
07:39:13,910 --> 07:39:16,310
most of the support struggle happens.

9052
07:39:16,310 --> 07:39:22,390
And so that in combination with the compounding piece leads us to this really cool fourth

9053
07:39:22,390 --> 07:39:24,710
section, which is activation.

9054
07:39:24,710 --> 07:39:28,390
And so a lot of you probably know your wow moment at this point.

9055
07:39:28,390 --> 07:39:32,470
You know when your customer is activated, you know when they're going to stick around.

9056
07:39:32,470 --> 07:39:34,350
And so how do you incentivize more of that, right?

9057
07:39:34,350 --> 07:39:36,150
How do you decrease time to value?

9058
07:39:36,150 --> 07:39:40,950
One of the easiest ways to do that is to give people money so that they get there.

9059
07:39:40,950 --> 07:39:42,710
It doesn't have to be much, right?

9060
07:39:42,710 --> 07:39:46,990
Just getting them across that hump is what turns people into great customers.

9061
07:39:46,990 --> 07:39:53,310
I have hooked up this bot to actually do the work and when an activation event happens,

9062
07:39:53,310 --> 07:39:55,550
where in this case, again, I'm using a note taking app.

9063
07:39:55,550 --> 07:40:01,590
If a template is shared with your teammates, we have $1,000, which is a crazy example,

9064
07:40:01,590 --> 07:40:02,590
ready to send.

9065
07:40:02,590 --> 07:40:10,590
automatically some of that email with those credits so that user or that customer can leverage those credits and they feel rewarded in that moment.

9066
07:40:10,590 --> 07:40:23,590
And so instead of you having to monitor every single customer's journey and do this manually or taking a tool and building it from scratch, you can just offload it to your bot and not think about it again and it will run the campaign on its own.

9067
07:40:23,590 --> 07:40:30,100
Okay, there are a few other pieces that are pretty obvious around the end-to-end customer journey, right?

9068
07:40:30,100 --> 07:40:34,100
