07:50:50,050 --> 07:50:54,050
So this bot has one purpose and one purpose only.

9259
07:50:54,050 --> 07:50:57,450
It is built and exists to talk like me.

9260
07:50:57,450 --> 07:51:00,970
So it looks through my emails, Slack, I message,

9261
07:51:00,970 --> 07:51:03,570
any other form of communication that I've done.

9262
07:51:03,570 --> 07:51:06,810
And it learns from how I talk.

9263
07:51:06,810 --> 07:51:08,010
And it doesn't just learn once.

9264
07:51:08,010 --> 07:51:10,050
I think this comes back to the compounding piece.

9265
07:51:10,050 --> 07:51:11,330
It learns over time.

9266
07:51:11,330 --> 07:51:13,970
So every week or so, or you can set it to whatever schedule

9267
07:51:13,970 --> 07:51:16,930
you want, it will take everything I've sent for the day

9268
07:51:16,930 --> 07:51:18,970
because it has access to all those tools.

9269
07:51:18,970 --> 07:51:21,270
And essentially learn from them and get better over time.

9270
07:51:21,270 --> 07:51:24,890
So now I can trust this bot to go and talk as me.

9271
07:51:24,890 --> 07:51:27,570
And what you'll notice is these other bots are actually

9272
07:51:27,570 --> 07:51:30,170
coming in and asking it for help.

9273
07:51:30,170 --> 07:51:32,850
So they are proactively bringing in

9274
07:51:32,850 --> 07:51:36,450
yeah bot to go talk like me across all of the different

9275
07:51:36,450 --> 07:51:37,290
surfaces.

9276
07:51:37,290 --> 07:51:39,170
And I don't need to do this myself.

9277
07:51:39,170 --> 07:51:41,250
After they do this a few times, or I encourage them,

9278
07:51:41,250 --> 07:51:44,890
like I said, they learn to loop in the other bots as needed.

9279
07:51:44,890 --> 07:51:46,610
And this bot might seem like a small one

9280
07:51:46,610 --> 07:51:47,850
because it's very simple.

9281
07:51:47,850 --> 07:51:53,690
But it's so important, especially if you're trying to do any sort of outbound or move quickly on communications.

9282
07:51:53,690 --> 07:51:56,810
It's nice to have a bot you can just trust to do this stuff.

9283
07:51:56,810 --> 07:51:59,170
Obviously you have some emails that are really sensitive.

9284
07:51:59,170 --> 07:52:02,930
So you might ask it to just keep them as drafts rather than just sending them right away.

9285
07:52:02,930 --> 07:52:13,000
But even then, it will learn from the delta between the draft it created and what was actually sent and get better and better over time with the end vision being that you don't need to think about it at all.

9286
07:52:13,000 --> 07:52:14,960
Okay, final tip.

9287
07:52:14,960 --> 07:52:18,000
I have a miscellaneous bot, and this bot has one job,

9288
07:52:18,000 --> 07:52:20,000
which is basically to be kind of a trash can

9289
07:52:20,000 --> 07:52:22,700
for all of the random requests I have.

9290
07:52:22,700 --> 07:52:25,120
Today I wanted to see if Drake's album dropped.

9291
07:52:25,120 --> 07:52:28,160
It is not yet sadly, but what's really cool about this one

9292
07:52:28,160 --> 07:52:30,000
is I can just ask it random things

9293
07:52:30,000 --> 07:52:32,400
without polluting the context of the other bots.

9294
07:52:32,400 --> 07:52:34,640
And if it ever has any important tasks to do

9295
07:52:34,640 --> 07:52:36,640
where it needs to transfer that context,

9296
07:52:36,640 --> 07:52:39,520
I can just ask and say, hey, you learned about XYZ,

9297
07:52:39,520 --> 07:52:42,120
go tell prod bot about what you've learned

9298
07:52:42,120 --> 07:52:44,370
so that it can get better in the future.

9299
07:52:44,370 --> 07:52:46,050
Sadly, Drake's album is an out.

9300
07:52:46,050 --> 07:52:48,530
It checked Instagram, but who knows?

9301
07:52:48,530 --> 07:52:50,330
We'll get there maybe later tonight.

9302
07:52:50,330 --> 07:52:52,170
Okay, those were all my bots.

9303
07:52:52,170 --> 07:52:55,290
I think ProtoBot is still going.

9304
07:52:55,290 --> 07:52:57,050
It's kicking off a cloud agent

9305
07:52:57,050 --> 07:52:59,010
and hopefully it finishes sometime soon.

9306
07:52:59,010 --> 07:53:01,730
But you'll notice because it has access to Grockbot,

9307
07:53:01,730 --> 07:53:05,170
it can actually just take a look at the interface

9308
07:53:05,170 --> 07:53:07,050
without needing to go find it anywhere.

9309
07:53:07,050 --> 07:53:09,210
And it can drive it and queway it.

9310
07:53:09,210 --> 07:53:10,370
And as these tests happen,

9311
07:53:10,370 --> 07:53:13,570
it's very easily verifiable whether it's shipped

9312
07:53:13,570 --> 07:53:14,970
the right thing or not.

9313
07:53:14,970 --> 07:53:17,810
And so I think all of these bots are very powerful.

9314
07:53:17,810 --> 07:53:20,490
And most importantly, they're all powerful in conjunction.

9315
07:53:20,490 --> 07:53:23,090
So when close bot gets some feedback,

9316
07:53:23,090 --> 07:53:24,970
it can pass it to proto bot.

9317
07:53:24,970 --> 07:53:27,130
Or when prod bot is trying to get across

9318
07:53:27,130 --> 07:53:29,810
some of the key product decisions that we've made,

9319
07:53:29,810 --> 07:53:31,970
it can pass that context off to close bot

9320
07:53:31,970 --> 07:53:33,970
so that it can sell the right stuff.

9321
07:53:33,970 --> 07:53:36,050
And overall, I think the key framework

9322
07:53:36,050 --> 07:53:37,890
that you folks need to keep in mind

9323
07:53:37,890 --> 07:53:41,010
is you want to start to try and productize yourself

9324
07:53:41,010 --> 07:53:42,210
as much as possible.

9325
07:53:42,210 --> 07:53:45,510
and give away all of your Legos, no matter how delightful they are,

9326
07:53:45,510 --> 07:53:47,970
so that you can focus on the highest leverage thing.

9327
07:53:47,970 --> 07:53:49,890
Because that is what helps you win in a world

9328
07:53:49,890 --> 07:53:52,450
where everyone is shipping just as fast,

9329
07:53:52,450 --> 07:53:54,170
if not faster for now.

9330
07:53:54,170 --> 07:53:56,650
So keep all that in mind, but those are my bots.

9331
07:53:56,650 --> 07:53:59,580
Let's go back to the presentation.

9332
07:53:59,580 --> 07:54:02,510
Okay, some final pieces.

9333
07:54:02,510 --> 07:54:05,230
What we learned, let your bots run free.

9334
07:54:05,230 --> 07:54:06,470
I am going to say this forever.

9335
07:54:06,470 --> 07:54:09,950
Give them access to as much as you are possibly comfortable with

9336
07:54:09,950 --> 07:54:12,270
because that is the only way they will be able to do work

9337
07:54:12,270 --> 07:54:17,640
end to end. You want to invest in them. So you might find times where you need a course

9338
07:54:17,640 --> 07:54:22,320
correct abot. And with an agent you might have the instinct of, man, I spent too many tokens

9339
07:54:22,320 --> 07:54:26,920
on course correcting it. The context is polluted. Let me just get rid of it and start a new one.

9340
07:54:26,920 --> 07:54:30,720
In this case, your key advantage is that your bots get really good as you spend more time

9341
07:54:30,720 --> 07:54:36,320
with them. And obviously as the team has learned internally, the more time you spend, the

9342
07:54:36,320 --> 07:54:39,880
better you do. And so it's really important to really believe in your bots the same way

9343
07:54:39,880 --> 07:54:45,000
you would with employees. And the other piece to keep in mind here is the other way to invest in them

9344
07:54:45,000 --> 07:54:50,680
is by giving them really good skills and tools. So it's very easy to say, hey, make this cooler,

9345
07:54:50,680 --> 07:54:55,400
and that could be your prompt that you want your bot to execute on. But obviously it's not going

9346
07:54:55,400 --> 07:54:59,640
to do a great job, and it's going to probably get stuck somewhere and ask you a few questions.

9347
07:54:59,640 --> 07:55:04,440
The more intentionality you put behind that task in the first place, let's you repeat it over and

9348
07:55:04,440 --> 07:55:06,500
over again without that many hitches.

9349
07:55:06,500 --> 07:55:10,680
And then finally, it is worth you taking one to two hours

9350
07:55:10,680 --> 07:55:13,100
and just thinking about your day.

9351
07:55:13,100 --> 07:55:14,220
I know that sounds dumb.

9352
07:55:14,220 --> 07:55:15,860
I know you're like, I need to move quickly,

9353
07:55:15,860 --> 07:55:18,100
but it is so, so important to just take the time.

9354
07:55:18,100 --> 07:55:20,340
I don't care when, just do it and figure out

9355
07:55:20,340 --> 07:55:23,180
what you want to delegate.

9356
07:55:23,180 --> 07:55:24,820
Because doing that intentionally

9357
07:55:24,820 --> 07:55:27,780
will save you so many hours versus just spinning up

9358
07:55:27,780 --> 07:55:29,620
bots and hoping they do things for you

9359
07:55:29,620 --> 07:55:33,160
without having a true intent around what they should do.

9360
07:55:33,160 --> 07:55:36,920
Okay, now I have a bonus round with some tips and tricks.

9361
07:55:36,920 --> 07:55:39,200
I was watching the live stream earlier

9362
07:55:39,200 --> 07:55:41,200
and some people were like, this is expensive,

9363
07:55:41,200 --> 07:55:44,000
which is true in some ways, not true in others

9364
07:55:44,000 --> 07:55:45,760
and we're working on it.

9365
07:55:45,760 --> 07:55:48,400
But there are some really easy high leverage tips

9366
07:55:48,400 --> 07:55:50,220
that can make your life a lot easier.

9367
07:55:50,220 --> 07:55:53,520
The first is that browser use is super powerful

9368
07:55:53,520 --> 07:55:57,280
and it unblocks your bot from doing a lot of things

9369
07:55:57,280 --> 07:55:59,880
that it couldn't do if it didn't have MCPs or APIs

9370
07:55:59,880 --> 07:56:01,080
or some other connection.

9371
07:56:01,080 --> 07:56:04,040
But it's also expensive to run multiple times.

9372
07:56:04,040 --> 07:56:07,160
And the easiest way to solve for this

9373
07:56:07,160 --> 07:56:11,240
is to buy us towards using APIs and using interfaces

9374
07:56:11,240 --> 07:56:12,840
that people have already built

9375
07:56:12,840 --> 07:56:15,960
or to actually kind of hack it a little bit.

9376
07:56:15,960 --> 07:56:18,880
You can ask your bot to look at network requests

9377
07:56:18,880 --> 07:56:21,680
while it does a task once and then figure out

9378
07:56:21,680 --> 07:56:25,320
which APIs are being hit while it's doing that task.

9379
07:56:25,320 --> 07:56:28,040
And then go and start to just hit those directly

9380
07:56:28,040 --> 07:56:30,920
which takes way less time, first of all,

9381
07:56:30,920 --> 07:56:32,380
And it's also way more token efficient

9382
07:56:32,380 --> 07:56:34,640
because you are no longer needing to go through

9383
07:56:34,640 --> 07:56:37,160
the browser interface and you can just do it all directly.

9384
07:56:37,160 --> 07:56:38,380
So ask your bot.

9385
07:56:38,380 --> 07:56:40,040
And this is true for all optimizations

9386
07:56:40,040 --> 07:56:42,220
by the way that you guys have probably been thinking of

9387
07:56:42,220 --> 07:56:43,320
or taking notes on.

9388
07:56:43,320 --> 07:56:45,000
Always just ask your bot how to do it

9389
07:56:45,000 --> 07:56:47,080
because it will figure it out for you,

9390
07:56:47,080 --> 07:56:48,040
which is very nice.

9391
07:56:48,040 --> 07:56:51,500
But be wary of browser use more than once.

9392
07:56:51,500 --> 07:56:53,700
And if you can get around it and scale quickly,

9393
07:56:53,700 --> 07:56:55,610
you absolutely should.

9394
07:56:55,610 --> 07:56:57,650
Second piece, routines.

9395
07:56:57,650 --> 07:56:59,330
When I was looking through some of the data

9396
07:56:59,330 --> 07:57:02,450
around the frequency of routines that people set,

9397
07:57:02,450 --> 07:57:05,970
a little shocked, and it freaks me out how often

9398
07:57:05,970 --> 07:57:07,210
you guys are running things.

9399
07:57:07,210 --> 07:57:09,490
But I think the most important part about routines

9400
07:57:09,490 --> 07:57:10,570
is to audit them.

9401
07:57:10,570 --> 07:57:11,810
And you don't have to do this yourself.

9402
07:57:11,810 --> 07:57:13,850
Again, get a bot to do it for you.

9403
07:57:13,850 --> 07:57:17,610
But the most important piece is be very intentional

9404
07:57:17,610 --> 07:57:19,410
about how often your routines are running.

9405
07:57:19,410 --> 07:57:22,330
They're really powerful, but most people over index

9406
07:57:22,330 --> 07:57:23,970
on how often they need to be running.

9407
07:57:23,970 --> 07:57:25,770
And they think this routine is so important,

9408
07:57:25,770 --> 07:57:27,090
I need to run it every 15 minutes,

9409
07:57:27,090 --> 07:57:29,210
which comes out to 100 times a day.

9410
07:57:29,210 --> 07:57:31,290
So that is a very expensive routine.

9411
07:57:31,290 --> 07:57:34,050
See if you can be a little more nifty with them.

9412
07:57:34,050 --> 07:57:36,050
So it's not just running them fewer times.

9413
07:57:36,050 --> 07:57:38,850
If you really need a routine, try and run them on webhooks

9414
07:57:38,850 --> 07:57:41,570
or try and run them with some sort of inbound signal

9415
07:57:41,570 --> 07:57:44,530
that will let your bots actually take in an input

9416
07:57:44,530 --> 07:57:47,130
and then run it, rather than just having it blindly run

9417
07:57:47,130 --> 07:57:48,130
on a schedule.

9418
07:57:48,130 --> 07:57:50,770
So those two things alone will probably save you a bunch

9419
07:57:50,770 --> 07:57:51,450
and tokens.

9420
07:57:51,450 --> 07:57:52,970
I know there was some demand for that.

9421
07:57:52,970 --> 07:57:53,690
OK.

9422
07:57:53,690 --> 07:57:57,410
Even more final tips before they came me off stage.

9423
07:57:57,410 --> 07:57:58,290
Make a voice bot.

9424
07:57:58,290 --> 07:58:00,430
Obviously, I love mine.

9425
07:58:00,430 --> 07:58:01,910
Please do this for yourself.

9426
07:58:01,910 --> 07:58:06,090
It is the most underrated way to get words out to other people.

9427
07:58:06,090 --> 07:58:08,790
It's have a bot that copies your voice.

9428
07:58:08,790 --> 07:58:09,830
Import your cookies.

9429
07:58:09,830 --> 07:58:12,350
This lets you stay signed in across a lot of different tools.

9430
07:58:12,350 --> 07:58:16,430
And it also stops you from having to constantly take

9431
07:58:16,430 --> 07:58:19,190
over the bots computer and help out.

9432
07:58:19,190 --> 07:58:20,470
Group bots by expertise.

9433
07:58:20,470 --> 07:58:22,070
This is kind of a personal preference thing,

9434
07:58:22,070 --> 07:58:25,870
but I love having my bots grouped by what they do.

9435
07:58:25,870 --> 07:58:28,590
And so if a bot is really good at just handling a customer,

9436
07:58:28,590 --> 07:58:31,110
I will give it everything customer related.

9437
07:58:31,110 --> 07:58:34,430
And if a bot is really good at data analysis,

9438
07:58:34,430 --> 07:58:35,630
that will be its sole job.

9439
07:58:35,630 --> 07:58:38,190
Because sometimes there are weird compounding pieces

9440
07:58:40,090 --> 07:58:49,090
And so when you're giving it to what feel like completely different tasks, you can still get some of the compounding benefits as long as they all fall under the same expertise.

9441
07:58:49,090 --> 07:58:58,090
There are a few more on here, like great skills, which we talked about, how bots can learn from you, and then auto optimization routines. But I think the last one is also pretty important.

9442
07:58:58,090 --> 07:59:02,010
having a bot that just exists to optimize your other bots.

9443
07:59:02,010 --> 07:59:04,970
That means better routines, figuring out where they went wrong,

9444
07:59:04,970 --> 07:59:07,130
or where you had to ask multiple times for something,

9445
07:59:07,130 --> 07:59:08,970
and then making sure that doesn't happen again.

9446
07:59:08,970 --> 07:59:12,170
And overseeing how the other ones work and improving them

9447
07:59:12,170 --> 07:59:15,130
is way easier than having to do a lot of this yourself.

9448
07:59:15,130 --> 07:59:16,730
So save yourself the time.

9449
07:59:16,730 --> 07:59:19,050
You set it once and then you forget it, which is really nice.

9450
07:59:19,050 --> 07:59:20,490
And I don't see enough people doing that.

9451
07:59:22,680 --> 07:59:28,120
Okay, so that is close to the end of what we've been doing here.

9452
07:59:28,120 --> 07:59:31,120
Thank you for your time and attention.

9453
07:59:31,120 --> 07:59:33,120
I am going to leave a QR code for stockbot.

9454
07:59:33,120 --> 07:59:35,120
If you guys want to steal it, it's a fun one.

9455
07:59:35,120 --> 07:59:37,120
You should try and use it on us.

9456
07:59:37,120 --> 07:59:38,120
I think that would be cool.

9457
07:59:38,120 --> 07:59:39,120
I want to see what people come up with.

9458
07:59:39,120 --> 07:59:42,120
But I really appreciate everyone being around.

9459
07:59:42,120 --> 07:59:51,120
I think one of the coolest parts about these bots and where they're headed is just how creative you can be the.

9460
07:59:51,120 --> 07:59:57,990
the amount of different bots and different combinations of bots that I've seen has really

9461
07:59:57,990 --> 07:59:58,990
blown me away.

9462
07:59:58,990 --> 07:59:59,910
And I think founders of the

9463
08:00:00,000 --> 08:00:04,000
perfect group to figure out the edges of this entire thing.

9464
08:00:04,000 --> 08:00:05,760
I don't think we've hit the limits yet.

9465
08:00:05,760 --> 08:00:08,120
And as we get closer and closer to figuring out

9466
08:00:08,120 --> 08:00:10,840
what these bots can actually do and what they can't,

9467
08:00:10,840 --> 08:00:13,080
we're gonna be looking for signal from you guys.

9468
08:00:13,080 --> 08:00:14,800
So really appreciate it.

9469
08:00:14,800 --> 08:00:16,880
If you are on the live stream,

9470
08:00:16,880 --> 08:00:20,080
we're gonna send you back to Matt Lauren in motion

9471
08:00:20,080 --> 08:00:22,400
to go and continue cooking.

9472
08:00:22,400 --> 08:00:30,210
So appreciate it, thanks.

9473
08:00:30,210 --> 08:00:32,810
Okay, for those of you here,

9474
08:00:32,810 --> 08:00:35,730
we will take 15 minutes and answer some questions

9475
08:00:35,730 --> 08:00:40,290
have. So we'll have some facilitators who maybe have mics if not just yell really loudly and we'll go

9476
08:00:40,290 --> 08:00:46,380
from there. So raise your hand if you have a question and we'll get after it. Yes, up here.

9477
08:00:49,070 --> 08:00:55,070
The idea of treating bots like humans, so you should spend one to two hours setting bots up. Do

9478
08:00:55,070 --> 08:00:59,790
you have a framework or suggestions as to how you actually do this? What's the way in which you

9479
08:01:01,380 --> 08:01:06,820
create jobs or roles and responsibilities for a bot? Yeah, the question is like what's the

9480
08:01:06,820 --> 08:01:09,260
the best way to set them up, essentially.

9481
08:01:09,260 --> 08:01:10,780
I think when you're trying to be intentional,

9482
08:01:10,780 --> 08:01:12,620
there are two things that matter.

9483
08:01:12,620 --> 08:01:15,020
One is figuring out what you need them for.

9484
08:01:15,020 --> 08:01:17,740
So actually inventoring every single thing

9485
08:01:17,740 --> 08:01:19,140
that you need to do is pretty important

9486
08:01:19,140 --> 08:01:21,180
because then you can start to group those things.

9487
08:01:21,180 --> 08:01:24,380
And like I said, I like my bots to be experts.

9488
08:01:24,380 --> 08:01:26,820
And so they will have a very specific domain

9489
08:01:26,820 --> 08:01:27,740
that they're good at.

9490
08:01:27,740 --> 08:01:29,460
And then they will expand their scope

9491
08:01:29,460 --> 08:01:31,980
as I have more questions for them outside of that domain.

9492
08:01:31,980 --> 08:01:33,940
And so I trust them to do things outside

9493
08:01:33,940 --> 08:01:35,260
of what they've been assigned.

9494
08:01:35,260 --> 08:01:38,700
But for the most part, I try to group them in,

9495
08:01:38,700 --> 08:01:41,060
you know, your finance bot or your job is,

9496
08:01:41,060 --> 08:01:43,820
you know, the customers or your job is like marketing generally.

9497
08:01:43,820 --> 08:01:45,220
And that's worked for me.

9498
08:01:45,220 --> 08:01:47,820
